(Product Manual  /  Chapter 1 Setup) Tj T*
(Press the power button for 3 seconds to start the device.) Tj T*
(Open Settings - Network, select Wi-Fi and finish pairing.) Tj T*
(Table: item=A value=42 ; item=B value=57) Tj T*
(Chapter 2 FAQ: If the answer is empty, check the uploaded documents.) Tj T*
(Contact: support@example.com  |  Staff ID: EMP-20260118) Tj T*
(Section 1.1 Indicator states: blue blinking means pairing mode is active.) Tj T*
(Section 1.2 Indicator states: solid green means the network is connected.) Tj T*
(Section 1.3 To reset the device, hold the button for at least 10 seconds.) Tj T*
(Section 1.4 After reset, all local settings return to factory defaults.) Tj T*
(Section 1.5 The default administrator account must be changed on first use.) Tj T*
(Section 1.6 Firmware updates are delivered over the air once per quarter.) Tj T*
(Section 1.7 Do not power off the device while a firmware update is running.) Tj T*
(Section 2.1 Upload a document from the Documents page before asking questions.) Tj T*
(Section 2.2 The parser extracts text, tables and page structure into chunks.) Tj T*
(Section 2.3 Each answer carries citations back to the original chunk ids.) Tj T*
(Section 2.4 If retrieval is empty, the assistant returns an honest fallback.) Tj T*
(Section 2.5 Badcase records can be exported by an administrator for review.) Tj T*
(Section 3.1 Sensitive identifiers are redacted before indexing and logging.) Tj T*
(Section 3.2 The four redaction gates share one rule set and one version tag.) Tj T*
(Section 3.3 Cache keys include authorization, data and policy version fields.) Tj T*
(Section 3.4 Restart recovery rebuilds volatile state from the truth layer.) Tj T*
(Section 4.1 This manual is a synthetic sample for offline demonstration only.) Tj T*
(Section 4.2 No real personal data appears in this generated document.) Tj
